cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Marketing Compliance Checker
message: >-
  If you use this software or its benchmark, please cite both the software and
  the accompanying article.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maragoudakis
    given-names: Manolis
    affiliation: Department of Informatics, Ionian University, Corfu, Greece
    email: mmarag@ionio.gr
repository-code: 'https://github.com/maragem/VA-marketSurveillance'
license: EUPL-1.2
abstract: >-
  A decision-support system that screens digital marketing campaigns against
  four EU legal instruments (AI Act, GDPR, DSA, UCPD) using GraphRAG over a
  curated legal knowledge graph and an agentic pipeline of regulation
  specialists. Agents may cite only provisions retrieved from the graph, which
  makes hallucination resistance a property of the architecture rather than of
  the model. Ships with a 52-campaign gold benchmark, a held-out split, a
  regulator-in-the-loop calibration loop, and archived result artifacts for
  every reported configuration.
keywords:
  - multimedia content governance
  - AI-generated media
  - synthetic media
  - digital advertising
  - legal natural language processing
  - large language model agent
  - GraphRAG
  - EU marketing law
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Regulator-in-the-Loop Compliance Screening: Graph-Grounded LLM Agents
      with a Continuously Calibrated Benchmark for EU Marketing Law
    # Author order as published in the article.
    authors:
      - family-names: Kaponis
        given-names: Alexios
      - family-names: Maragoudakis
        given-names: Manolis
    journal: Multimedia
    publisher:
      name: MDPI
    year: 2026
    volume: 2
